# The Blueprint builds with dockerContext: . (the repo root), because the
# Dockerfile needs both backend/ and knowledge/. Without this file the entire
# repo — .git history, the Xcode sources, and any local secrets or SQLite
# database — is uploaded to Render's builder on every deploy. None of it is
# COPYed into the image, but it should never leave the machine in the first
# place.

.git
.gitignore

# Secrets and local state. backend/.env is gitignored, so it exists only on
# your Mac — which is exactly where a build context would pick it up.
backend/.env
backend/.env.*
backend/data/
!backend/.env.example

# iOS client — never part of the server image.
ios/

# Docs and planning.
docs/
*.md
!knowledge/**/*.md

# Python and editor droppings.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.DS_Store
